@page
@model ConWatch.Pages.SetupModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Quick setup — ConnectionWatcher";
}

<h2>Quick setup</h2>
<p>
    Three steps and ConnectionWatcher is watching your internet connection —
    no typing required unless you want to change something.
    <a href="/Config/Targets">Skip setup and configure manually</a>.
</p>
<ul class="form-errors" id="errors"></ul>

<details id="clone-section">
    <summary>Moving from another ConnectionWatcher? Copy everything from it</summary>
    <p><small>Clones the source node's configuration (including any local LAN devices), full history, and (with its
    admin password) its notification secrets. This node arrives as a read-only
    copy while the source keeps monitoring; when it looks right, press
    <b>Take over</b> on the Settings page for a seconds-long hand-off.</small></p>
    <ul class="form-errors" id="clone-errors"></ul>
    <div class="grid">
        <label>Source URL
            <input id="clone-url" placeholder="https://conwatch.example.com/ or http://192.168.1.5:8080" />
        </label>
        <label>Source admin password <small>(leave empty if none is set)</small>
            <input id="clone-password" type="password" autocomplete="off" />
        </label>
    </div>
    <p><label><input id="clone-local" type="checkbox" checked />
        Also copy my local devices <small>(LAN devices tracked on the side — uncheck when this node is on a different network; taking over later keeps your choice)</small></label></p>
    <p><button id="clone-btn" type="button">Clone from this node</button>
       <span id="clone-progress"></span></p>
    <div id="clone-insecure" hidden>
        <article style="border-color: var(--cw-warn)">
            <p>⚠ <b>This would cross your network unencrypted.</b> The source's admin
            password would be sent — and its MQTT password and webhook URLs received —
            over plain HTTP. If the source has an HTTPS address, use that instead.</p>
            <p>
                <button id="clone-insecure-anyway" type="button" class="secondary">I understand — send it over HTTP</button>
                <button id="clone-no-secrets" type="button" class="secondary outline">Clone without secrets</button>
            </p>
            <p><small>"Without secrets" copies everything except the MQTT password and
            webhook/heartbeat URLs; you re-enter those on the Settings page before taking over.</small></p>
        </article>
    </div>
</details>

<section id="step-router">
    <h4>1 · Your router</h4>
    <p>
        Detected gateway candidates are listed below — confirm the right one.
        (Inside a container the detected gateway can be the container's bridge,
        not your router; if unsure, check your computer's network settings.)
    </p>
    <div id="gateway-list" aria-busy="true">searching…</div>
    <div class="grid">
        <label>Name <input id="router-name" value="Router" /></label>
        <label>Address <input id="router-address" placeholder="192.168.1.1" /></label>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="step-anchors">
    <h4>2 · Internet anchors</h4>
    <p>
        These public anycast DNS resolvers are built for public traffic; at the
        polite Public cadence each sees about six pings per minute from you.
        Several anchors let ConnectionWatcher tell "one site is having a bad
        day" apart from real internet weather.
    </p>
    <div id="anchor-list" aria-busy="true">loading…</div>
</section>

<section id="step-wan">
    <h4>3 · Your router's public address <small>(optional)</small></h4>
    <p>
        Monitoring the router's outside (WAN) address separates "my Wi-Fi/router
        works" from "my internet line works".
    </p>
    <button id="wan-probe" class="outline" type="button">Find my router's public address</button>
    <div id="wan-result"></div>
    <label style="margin-top: 0.8rem">Who is your internet provider? <small>(optional — lets reports
        and alerts say "Comcast is down" instead of naming a router)</small>
        <input id="isp-name" placeholder="e.g. Comcast, Starlink" />
    </label>
</section>

<p>
    <button id="apply" type="button">Start monitoring</button>
</p>

@section Scripts {
    <script src="~/lib/site-config.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
    <script src="~/lib/site-setup.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
}
